WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
- My next guest is a living
legend in the world of racing.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.680
He's a seven time NASCAR champion

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.900
and five of those wins, back
to back to back to back.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:10.733
That's right.

00:00:10.733 --> 00:00:12.830
Something that's never been done before.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.800
Now at 45 years old, he is a rookie again

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.930
this time in the world
of Indy race car driving.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.291
So everybody welcome my
friend, Jimmy Johnson.

00:00:20.291 --> 00:00:24.541
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:29.852
I wish I could hug you.

00:00:29.852 --> 00:00:30.685
I know.

00:00:30.685 --> 00:00:31.518
I know it's so weird.

00:00:31.518 --> 00:00:32.720
We can't hug yet.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.553
- I know.

00:00:33.553 --> 00:00:34.720
- We're not there yet,
but we're getting close.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.770
- Soon. I know, right?
- Yes.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:36.610
How are you?

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:37.443
- I'm fantastic.

00:00:37.443 --> 00:00:38.276
I hope you are too.

00:00:38.276 --> 00:00:39.109
- I am.

00:00:39.109 --> 00:00:40.106
I'm doing all right.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.980
And you were here like
a year ago, I believe.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.420
And you announced you're retiring.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:44.710
So you were like, nope, just kidding.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:45.543
- Psych.

00:00:45.543 --> 00:00:46.376
- You're like those
musicians that are like

00:00:46.376 --> 00:00:47.750
it's my farewell tour, but it's not.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:48.630
- It's not, no.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.118
And I was thinking about
it before I came out

00:00:51.118 --> 00:00:53.000
and I knew you were
gonna ask me about that.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.480
And, you know, I don't think like yourself

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.150
I don't think you can ever stop singing

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:58.450
or playing or being with the band.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:02.030
So what I was ready to step
away from was the grind

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:05.470
of the 38 races a year that
I did for 20 plus years.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:07.120
So kinda like being out on the road,

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.450
I guess for you and touring and stuff.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.690
But now I have a much
shorter schedule for racing

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.170
and having a blast doing it.

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.320
- So for the idiots in the room,

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.240
what's the difference
between NASCAR and Indy?

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.280
- I know I've been to both.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.320
I can see there's a difference

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.173
but what is like the biggest difference?

00:01:24.173 --> 00:01:27.900
- From an aesthetic standpoint,
one's a big sedan vehicle.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.930
And then the Indy car is
this little lightweight

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:31.340
like rocket ship that you drive.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.336
And literally the weight of the vehicle

00:01:33.336 --> 00:01:36.240
would make the Indy
car, like a sports car.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.850
And then the NASCAR vehicle
would be much more like an SUV.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:42.750
- So wait, does that make
it more or less dangerous?

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.667
- Dangers probably pretty equal.

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:47.010
But the experience of driving
the car is much different.

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:49.520
The Indy car, it takes a lot of aggression

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.530
and the car doesn't ever give up.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:54.000
Like you can't hurt the tires,
you can't hurt the brakes.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.100
And the intensity is
much higher driving it.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.206
With the NASCAR vehicle it's a bigger car.

00:01:58.206 --> 00:02:00.530
You can wear the brakes out in a race,

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:01.510
you can hurt the tires

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:03.330
and you have to finesse it a bit more.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.163
- Okay.

00:02:04.163 --> 00:02:05.350
So has this ever been done?

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:06.990
Has anybody ever gone from NASCAR,

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:10.330
especially on such a huge successful level

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.090
and then been like,
no, I'm gonna try Indy.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.320
Has anyone ever done that?

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.440
- There may have been somebody

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.440
in the seventies I'm told but yeah,

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.648
nothing recently
- I've never heard of that.

00:02:17.648 --> 00:02:19.790
- We've had more open-wheel drivers

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:22.140
try NASCAR in recent time,

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.310
but really not the other direction.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.105
And honestly, this was a
childhood dream of mine.

00:02:25.105 --> 00:02:26.930
Growing up on the West coast,

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:31.490
Indy car during my generation
was the big sport to,

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:33.240
you know, want to race
in and aspire to be in.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.730
So my world changed when my manufacturer

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:37.563
that I drove for said,

00:02:37.563 --> 00:02:39.550
"Hey, look we're not gonna
be in Indy Car any longer.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.920
You need to move to North
Carolina and go stock car racing."

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.390
And my path was set then.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:44.251
- Wow.

00:02:44.251 --> 00:02:46.330
- Yeah, but come back
to it now is super cool.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:47.420
- I know I was getting,

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.100
and this is, it sounds like a movie.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.277
Like I was reading about
you last night and was like,

00:02:51.277 --> 00:02:55.283
"This sounds like a great
plot for a movie, by the way."

00:02:55.283 --> 00:02:57.470
I was like, it's just, I would watch.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:59.540
So are you starting to see that your girls

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:00.900
are daredevils like you?

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.210
And does it scare you?

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:03.350
Cause it's not, you it's them.

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:04.183
- True.

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:06.857
It is far harder watching my children

00:03:06.857 --> 00:03:08.940
do things that I love to do.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.830
And I know that they're into than me

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.040
participating in it myself.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.544
But we're a very active family in skiing.

00:03:14.544 --> 00:03:17.310
My girls both ride horses
and are jumping horses.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.270
We have dirt bikes.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.160
- Oh, they're doing all the things

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.100
to maybe possibly end up
with a broken collarbone.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.050
- Correct, but I wanna think

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:25.720
that the combination of mom's
cautious approach to things

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.590
and then my crazy approach
will balance them out.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.010
- Okay, balance is good.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:29.960
- Balance is good.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.800
- So how does it feel to
have fans back in the stands?

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:33.633
- It's been great.

00:03:33.633 --> 00:03:35.569
I mean, I think at one point in time

00:03:35.569 --> 00:03:37.990
I was very eager just to work again

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:39.580
and to be back on the track

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.920
and know that our sport was on television.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.830
And then fans have slowly been coming back

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.090
and now with the direction COVID has gone,

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:49.130
to actually have, you
know, half of a stadium

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.960
filled full of fans is such a great site.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:52.930
And the energy that they bring,

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.090
is unbelievable.
- The energy is crazy.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:57.420
- I've been to Indy and
NASCAR and it is nuts.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.253
- It is fun.

00:03:58.253 --> 00:04:00.470
- Like you cannot help, I have no idea

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:01.460
generally what's going on,

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.420
and I'm just like, wow!

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.010
Because it's just a good time.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.503
It's like a country music festival.

00:04:06.503 --> 00:04:08.000
You don't even have to know the music.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.560
You're just having a good time.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.350
So, and fans, they get to vote.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.183
Is it on your car?

00:04:12.183 --> 00:04:13.410
The color of your car?

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:15.130
- Yeah, so there's a
really neat opportunity.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.870
If people want to learn more
about it, go to carvana.com.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:20.210
And of course, we're
always trying to figure out

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.400
how to integrate with the fans.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.169
And now that fans are back in the stands,

00:04:23.169 --> 00:04:25.931
we just want them to know
that they can have ownership

00:04:25.931 --> 00:04:28.225
in a car that I'm gonna race at some point

00:04:28.225 --> 00:04:29.610
during the season.
- Which is cool

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.390
- So we'll have five times in total

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.140
and there'll be three
more opportunities left

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:35.250
for the fans to pick what
my race car looks like.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.120
- Wait, so what color so far then?

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.610
Like, what are, do you have any?

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.020
Cause green is a great color.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.350
Kelly Green is a great thing

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:42.183
- I understand.

00:04:42.183 --> 00:04:45.270
But Carvana blue is a better
color for my situation.

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:46.247
- Okay, well, you know what?

00:04:46.247 --> 00:04:49.610
I like blue too though, because
it's the winning ribbon.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:51.690
It's the, blue is the winning ribbon.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:52.523
- Yeah.

00:04:52.523 --> 00:04:53.356
- You're projecting.
- You're projecting, yeah.

00:04:53.356 --> 00:04:54.189
- I like it, I like it.

00:04:54.189 --> 00:04:55.411
But Kelly Green is still a great color.

00:04:55.411 --> 00:04:59.140
So you can see Jimmy Johnson
race at the GMR Grand Prix

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:00.850
at the Indianapolis Motor Speedway.

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:02.010
This Saturday, May 15th.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:02.843
You got to check it out.

00:05:02.843 --> 00:05:05.140
Also be sure to check
out Jimmy in the booth

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.810
for NBC's coverage of the Indianapolis 500

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:08.953
on Sunday, May 30th.

